{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478996-1st-edition-books-that-work-with-2nd-edition","id":478996,"title":"1st edition books that work with 2nd edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-13T06:29:22-07:00","id":478996,"title":"1st edition books that work with 2nd edition","content":"HI,<br /> I'm working my way through Vampire the Requiem 2nd edition and I'm loving it. I am not new to WoD and I read 1st edition when it was released. And while I loved certain things about it I was not blown away as I have been with 2nd Ed. So much stuff jumps off the page and screams 'PLAY ME&quot;. I was never fond of Gangrel or Daeva, but the write ups in 2nd ed made me want to play them. The same with the Covenants, Carthians and Invictus were never interesting to me, but now they rock.<br /> <br /> I have been looking at the various other books in the Requiem line and a lot of them sound fascinating. However, I don't want to buy books where the fluff is out of sync with 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> For example. Are the Covenant books still relevant? Was the change between the Covenants in 1st and 2nd so drastic that the books are no longer useful?<br /> <br /> So, what books work best with 2nd ed and which don't?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5675-jivewookiee","name":"Jivewookiee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T07:18:45-07:00","id":479027,"title":"","content":"I think it says it in the introduction. The clan books and Damnation City, at least.<br /> <br /> Glad you're enjoying the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:35:24-07:00","id":479071,"title":"","content":"The Blood Sorcery book too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:21:43-07:00","id":479398,"title":"","content":"I think the Covenant books are still <i>mostly</i> useful, as long as you keep in mind that where the sources disagree, 2e wins. The upcoming Secrets of the Covenants may change that. The Clan books are still good, Blood Sorcery is still good, with some slight changes mentioned in a sidebar in 2e. Damnation City still works, though obviously Haven Size should be replaced with Housing, Haven Security should be replaced with Safe Place, and Haven Location should be replaced with Feeding Grounnds. Bloodline books can still be used - although old bloodlines may not have been written under 2e design philosophy, their mechanics are still pretty much compatible with the rules changes. I think Ancient Mysteries is still essentially reliable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:26:07-07:00","id":479403,"title":"","content":"The Danse Macabre, Invite Only, Strange Dead Love, Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners, Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, Ancient Mysteries, Ancient Bloodlines, New Wave Requiem, Requiem for Rome, Fall of the Camarilla...<br /> <br /> Tone-wise, pretty much everything published after Damnation City reads more like a 2e than a 1e product. General fan consensus is that Requiem really established its own identity (as opposed to being Masquerade Lite) after that point.<br /> <br /> You can tell because the post-Damnation City books have red instead of gray backgrounds, too. Color-coded for your convenience!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:48:56-07:00","id":479676,"title":"","content":"How can you not like Gangrel?<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting... Go Wolverine on those bitches!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T05:45:00-07:00","id":596791,"title":"","content":"How about CotD: New Orleans? Would you need to change much for it to be a valid chronicle in a can?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5675-jivewookiee","name":"Jivewookiee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T06:08:02-07:00","id":596803,"title":"","content":"I've personally run New Orleans as year long Blood and Smoke chronicle without much problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:10:03-07:00","id":602063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jivewookiee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478996-1st-edition-books-that-work-with-2nd-edition?p=596791#post596791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about CotD: New Orleans? Would you need to change much for it to be a valid chronicle in a can?</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of details about NPCs don't really work and need to be adjusted, mostly related to the way the Sanctified have changed since early 1e. I'd also make Baron Cimiti\u00e8re's crew its own local Covenant instead of trying to cram them into the Circle. Apart from that, the vast majority of stuff works right out of the book, including most of the stats for NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T09:02:55-07:00","id":602974,"title":"","content":"I don't think they need to be changed. The covenants take different forms in diferents places. The catholicism from Lancea et Sanctum from New Orleans could be just a local element enforced by personal views from Savoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:24:06-07:00","id":611172,"title":"","content":"You mean Vidal? The problem is too deep to wave away as local variation. The Sanctified religion is fundamentally incompatible with practicing mortal Christianity. The <i>Testament</i> specifically forbids it. I also doubt Morrow would be allowed to be a priest with a mortal congregation, but that's at least debatable. What's not debatable is the idea that Vidal would still identify as a Catholic in the sense that living people do (as opposed to thinking it's the true faith for mortals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:39:52-07:00","id":611210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478996-1st-edition-books-that-work-with-2nd-edition?p=611172#post611172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also doubt Morrow would be allowed to be a priest with a mortal congregation, but that's at least debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Sanctified are forbidden from doing this sort of thing, though I could imagine Morrow having a priestly aesthetic isn't out of the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T05:28:11-07:00","id":612098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jivewookiee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478996-1st-edition-books-that-work-with-2nd-edition?p=596791#post596791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about CotD: New Orleans? Would you need to change much for it to be a valid chronicle in a can?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say the biggest problem with running CotD New Orleans is working on how the city was affected by Katrina. There's also a new Voodoo covenant-type thing in Ancient Mysteries, I think it was? <br /> <br /> All in all, you can use it, but there's a lot of dated material in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}